      "id": "sol.amc-10a-2024-p5.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Factor \\(2024 = 2^3 \\cdot 11 \\cdot 23.\\) The prime \\(23\\) is the bottleneck: for \\(23\\) to divide \\(n!,\\) we need \\(n \\ge 23.\\) At \\(n = 23,\\) the product \\(23!\\) already has \\(23,\\) \\(11,\\) and plenty of factors of \\(2,\\) so \\(23!\\) is divisible by \\(2024.\\) The least value is \\(23.\\) Thus, D is the correct answer.",
